{"id":52,"text":"Anna was seventeen when her best friend, Julia, moved to another country. They promised to write to each other every month.\n\nAnna wrote her first letter the following week. She waited and waited for an answer, but nothing arrived. After three months, she stopped writing. “She has forgotten me,” she thought bitterly.\n\nTwenty years passed. Anna became a nurse and married. One day, she was cleaning her mother’s attic when she found a small box. Inside there were twelve letters, all addressed to her, all in Julia’s handwriting.\n\nHer hands began to shake. Her mother had hidden them, perhaps because she was afraid Anna would leave too. Anna read them one by one, crying and laughing at the same time. In each letter, Julia asked the same question: “Why don’t you write to me?”\n\nThat evening, Anna searched for Julia on the internet. After an hour, she found her. She wrote a short message: “I never forgot you. I only found your letters today.”\n\nAn answer came within minutes. “I never forgot you either. I have been waiting for twenty years.”\n\nThree weeks later, they met at an airport and held each other without saying a word.\n\nMoral: It’s never too late to repair a friendship.","tr":null,"gl":{"anna":"Anna (ism)","was":"edi","seventeen":"o'n yetti","when":"qachon; -ganda","her":"uni; uning (ayol)","best":"eng yaxshi","friend":"do'st","julia":"Yuliya (ism)","moved":"qimirladi; ko'chdi","to":"-ga; uchun","another":"boshqa, yana bir","country":"mamlakat","they":"ular","promised":"va'da berdi","write":"yozmoq","each":"har bir","other":"boshqa","every":"har","month":"oy","wrote":"yozdi","first":"birinchi; avval","letter":"xat; harf","the":"(aniq artikl)","following":"keyingi","week":"hafta","she":"u (ayol)","waited":"kutdi","and":"va","for":"uchun; davomida","an":"bir (noaniq artikl)","answer":"javob","but":"lekin, ammo","nothing":"hech narsa","arrived":"yetib keldi","after":"keyin, so'ng","three":"uch","months":"oylar","stopped":"to'xtadi","writing":"